        "original_id": "298c3850-e98f-51d1-8197-304a0c4b8654",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Time Warner, Turner Broadcasting\n- TV Channels: Boomerang, Cartoon Network\n- Franchises and Shows: Scooby-Doo, Looney Tunes, Tom and Jerry, Sonic Boom, The Powerpuff Girls, The Magilla Gorilla Show\n- Organizations: Hanna-Barbera Productions\n- People: Joe Ruby, Ken Spears\n\nFacts:\n- Scooby-Doo was created for Hanna-Barbera Productions by writers Joe Ruby and Ken Spears in 1969.\n- Scooby-Doo is an American animated cartoon franchise that has comprised several animated television series produced from 1969 to the present.\n- Boomerang specializes in classic and contemporary animated programming from Time Warner's archive, including Looney Tunes, Tom and Jerry, and Scooby-Doo.\n- Boomerang also airs repeats of in-production series from its sister channel and fellow Turner-owned channel, Cartoon Network, including Sonic Boom and The Powerpuff Girls.\n- The Magilla Gorilla Show aired on Boomerang until July 22, 2012.",
